67,20411,121,2.361,1.866,[[2,0.579,33,69],[9,0.421,53,52]],[["fb61cf1e_63da8f05",26,-1,1,"nit: I believe this can be `const Profile* profile`"]],0,339],[7170604,20411,22,0.737,0.556,[[2,34]],[],0,340],[7167192,20412,372,7.601,6.192,[[2,0.836,35,314],[20,0.14,8,51],[5,0.024,1,7]],[["8b00af93_f7a27afe",47,-1,1,"nit: Should this also be `constexpr`? (here and elsewhere)"],["9eb34717_26c4cd75",53,-1,1,"trivial nit: `const base::TimeTicks` (also below)"],["a3fe00f1_827c8c5e",40,-1,1,"nit: Should this return `MetricsReporter&`?"]],0,341],[7078070,20418,125,2.361,1.866,[[2,0.969,36,123],[28,0.016,12,1],[32,0.016,1,1]],[],0,342],[7210707,20432,558,16.15,13.645,[[41,0.608,0,342],[30,0.291,4,164],[8,0.026,42,14],[10,0.025,10,13],[31,0.021,5,10],[29,0.019,58,10],[2,0.011,37,5]],[["062c2901_9e5e869a",54,-6,1,"This looks wrong. The path should never contains the scheme and the host. Otherwise, it may conflict with the source's origin. For example `colors.css` should belong to the LocalResourceSource with…"],["46241eb3_ae92eb29",55,-6,1,"Can we move these line to L265 where they are actually used?"],["49d00ee7_62c6db2e",56,-6,0,"Since it's not used outside of `//content`, can you move it to `content/common/features.h`?"],["52faca2d_024a0717",54,-6,0,"The duplication here is a bit unfortunate. Do you think it's possible to send a more complete map, then generate the response body string for `string.m.js` for that in the renderer (like you…"],["7c50b185_06ca3699",55,-6,0,"optiona: this function has 2 branches: generated resources and resource bundle resource, can we make helper functions to serve resource bundle resource as well? That will make the branches more…"],["ab89880c_8d4a667b",49,-6,1,"It is unclear how the loading will be optimized. Can we make the flag name a bit more descriptive, e.g. `kWebUIInProcResourceLoadingV2`? This is a continuation of the launched in-proc resource…"],["b628d035_b434d230",57,-6,1,"We probably don't want the path key to contain the host. See my comment in `local_resource_loader_config.mojom`"],["bb4d9ce8_b2813aa3",58,-6,1,"It seems that this is not actually used?"],["c9f6181b_538ed8dc",55,-6,1,"Why is this needed? I have the impression that every resource has an origin. e.g., colors.css must be served from `chrome://theme/colors.css` and it cannot be served from…"],["ca8b4137_709e3be5",59,-6,1,"This looks like a duplicate of L122-L124."],["cbcd1022_bbc3ecf6",59,-6,1,"optional: leave a comment to explain the check, e.g., ```suggestion // CHECKs that dynamic resources (e.g., string.m.js) do not have a resource id. for (auto& [path, content] : *path_to_response_map)…"],["d93026aa_ef3186f8",60,-6,1,"\"different\" is probably not accurate - it might be mis-interpreted as two features are independent, where actually the new feature relies on the old feature being enabled. What about something like :…"],["e6d500cd_4893560d",61,-6,1,"It seems that this is not actually used?"],["58d39370_398af7ff",59,-5,1,"I think this should be a configurable property on a `URLDataSources`, e.g. `URLDataSources::set_load_in_process(bool)`. Maybe leave a TODO?"],["16e9fbfd_8b86737a",54,-2,1,"Does this mean map<string, union{uint32, string}> conceptually, so that uniqueness of the key will be guaranteed? If so, can we introduce a union type for the case?"],["05df03b1_8fc09c6c",55,-1,1,"Duplicate line"],["4321dda3_8fcef88a",57,-1,1,"Let's add a comment that this not actually doing any replacement is expected"],["54db8abf_98cd13c9",62,-1,1,"Are there actually other resources that use `kStringsJsPath`?"],["fc3821f6_0a43abc8",55,-1,0,"So we're skipping doing string replacements, because I guess `string.js` and `colors.css` doesn't actually need replacement (or have done replacement in the browser)? Maybe good to point that out in…"],["8ed6b4b7_ddbebf8e",63,0,1,"Huh, it looks like we can get here at `WILL_PROCESS_RESPONSE` time as well. I guess you would need to check `request->state()` and call `GetOriginToCommit()` if it's already reached…"],["ed0c79d8_cf3ee598",64,0,1,"Should this be removed?"],["fa14c34f_c2fd750b",59,0,1,"Sorry I missed this, just noticed when writing a test on top of this change. This isn't the correct origin, since `frame_host_` can still be a speculative RenderFrameHost with no committed origin…"]],0,343],[7255577,20434,11,0.421,0.3,[[2,38]],[],0,344],[7251727,20440,428,7.601,6.192,[[2,0.551,39,234],[41,0.412,1,178],[10,0.032,11,13],[31,0.005,6,1]],[["1ac29803_a3a66f51",65,-3,1,"Old line?"],["330f3c49_1a90dfde",66,-3,1,"So we call this \"shared\" because eventually the CSS will not be generated on every call of this like it currently does, but once in a shared location?"],["384c785c_bf8c818a",61,-3,1,"I don't think this term is used elsewhere (which seems to use \"shared\"?), can you expand on this?"],["5905c427_fe073010",66,-3,1,"Why is this called `visitor`?"],["7d64ba8b_90edea05",46,-3,1,"But will this get updated when that happens? If the theme changes and a new window is created, will it use this value too? (I guess right now we get the CSS on every call, but might be useful to test…"],["9455a8f7_e31ad21f",65,-3,1,"nit: add param name comment here and below"],["ded9a0fd_c70798dc",61,-3,1,"As someone who's not very familiar with this: Why don't we want to add it here?"],["023afc40_4084debe",67,-2,1,"Here and a few other places: No need to check for `theme_service` here. It is guaranteed to be non-null (browser_widget.cc L452)."],["057fb1fa_03f9b62b",67,-2,1,"Here and at L132, the original code does not treat `is_incognito` specially. Is there a reason for these handlings?"],["1ebdc199_0dfbef82",67,-2,1,"ditto."],["33255780_d9bd74e1",66,-2,1,"optional: CHECK that `origin` key does not exist in `sources` to prevent accidental overwrites."],["3abce360_f56429f1",61,-2,1,"Should we be returning a `base::MakeRefCounted` here?"],["3df6b8ad_db8afd70",68,-2,1,"`is_grayscale` and `is_baseline` is part of ColorProviderKey. If we can get `ColorProviderKey` from a WebContents that will